Hi Distance group,

Eric Rexstad recently helped me follow up on my original question regarding cluster size bias using observation team as a covariate (with a total of 10 different teams). I'd like to share this off-list exchange since posting my original question in case others have the same issue.

To summarise, he suggested that either adjustment terms or covariates should be used in a model, but not both, and he wrote code to test for cluster size bias in models with a multi-level factor covariate (attached). His code is written for a half normal key function but we also discuss what the code would look like for the hazard rate function. Other code <http://www.creem.st-and.ac.uk/ericr/sizebias.html> available on this group addresses a similar issue  <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/distance-sampling/cluster$20size$20bias%7Csort:relevance/distance-sampling/8Kk12EOg-cY/dakcI3y8-xMJ>but with two binary covariates.

Many thanks to Eric for taking the time to help!
Michelle

